WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.724
Express and other Node.

00:00:01.724 --> 00:00:05.378
js frameworks make it easy to receive request data,

00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:09.032
but they do not automatically know the application's rules.

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:12.279
Request bodies, path parameters, query parameters, headers, cookies,

00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:15.121
and file metadata all need explicit expectations.

00:00:15.121 --> 00:00:17.151
Middleware can help centralize validation,

00:00:17.151 --> 00:00:22.429
but each route should still have a clear contract for what it accepts.

00:00:22.429 --> 00:00:25.677
Frontend form validation should align with server validation.

00:00:25.677 --> 00:00:30.143
A form might enforce required fields, length, and format for usability,

00:00:30.143 --> 00:00:33.390
while the API enforces the same rules authoritatively.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.826
When frontend and backend rules diverge,

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:42.322
users get confusing errors and attackers get opportunities to submit data the server did not expect.

00:00:42.322 --> 00:00:45.570
Shared schema patterns can help reduce that drift.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.006
URL and route parameters need context.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:52.878
A value that looks like an identifier may still need to match

00:00:52.878 --> 00:00:55.313
the authenticated user's tenant or permissions.

00:00:55.313 --> 00:00:59.779
Headers and cookies may require format checks, signature verification, expiration checks,

00:00:59.779 --> 00:01:00.997
and safe parsing.

00:01:00.997 --> 00:01:05.463
Uploaded files need validation of size, name, declared type, detected content,

00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:07.899
storage location, and later access behavior.

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:12.365
GraphQL and WebSocket inputs deserve the same care as REST APIs.

00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:13.989
GraphQL schemas describe operations,

00:01:13.989 --> 00:01:17.236
but authorization and business rules still need enforcement.

00:01:17.236 --> 00:01:22.108
WebSocket messages are long-lived external input and should be parsed, typed, size-limited,

00:01:22.108 --> 00:01:24.138
and validated by message type.

00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:26.980
Every protocol boundary is a validation boundary.
